        "Abstract": "This paper constructs a new Japanese speech corpus called JTubeSpeech from YouTube videos and subtitles for speech recognition and speaker verification. The corpus is constructed using a mostly language-independent strategy, employing CTC-based techniques for ASR and a speaker variation-based method for ASV. The corpus includes 1,300 hours of data for Japanese ASR and 900 hours for ASV."
